---
pagination:
  data: collections.profiles
  size: 1
  alias: profile
permalink: "/profiles/{{ profile.slug }}/"
layout: layouts/profile.njk
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ profile.display_name | safe }}"
  description: "Profile of {{ profile.display_name | safe }}, named in public records on DPRK cyber operations, at confidence level {{ profile.confidence_level | safe }}. All claims sourced to the records cited on this page."
---
{#
  src/profiles/profile-page.njk — thin pagination shim
  ======================================================

  This file has (deliberately) almost no body. Its only job is to paginate
  over the `profiles` collection (registered in .eleventy.js via
  eleventyConfig.addCollection("profiles", ...), which reads every
  src/profiles/*.json file)
  and, for each one, render src/_includes/layouts/profile.njk with that
  profile bound to the `profile` variable. All actual profile-page markup
  lives in layouts/profile.njk, not here.

  `eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true` keeps this template file itself
  out of any 11ty tag-based collection (it is not itself a profile - it is
  the generator of N profile pages).
#}
